<title>BELGIUM: EU clears aid to Alitalia, imposes conditions.</title>
<headline>EU clears aid to Alitalia, imposes conditions.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission cleared the payment of 2.75 trillion lire ($1.6 billion) of state to Italian flag carrier Alitalia on Tuesday, imposing various conditions in return for approval of the state-funded injection.</p>
<p>Aid clearance, widely signalled in advance after the successful conclusion of negotiations between the Commission and the Rome government, included a requirement that the airline sell its holding in the Hungarian carrier MALEV, a statement said.</p>
</text>
